// INTERFACE assertions — what the C compiler is TOLD, not how the body is spelled.
//
// These three tests are the residue of a family that used to grep the OLD emitter's private
// names (`__match`, `__try`, `__elsev`). Those pinned an IMPLEMENTATION, and the project now has
// two: every one of them failed against the new backend while the programs behaved identically.
// The behaviour is asserted by the sibling `.expected` oracle, and by `emit_gate`, which runs
// all 399 programs through BOTH backends and compares.
//
// What is left here is the part neither of those covers: the SIGNATURE. Patterns are chosen to
// hold for either backend — the qualifiers and attributes that carry a proof, never a parameter
// NAME or a struct spelling.
//
// A borrow is exclusive (restrict), never null (nonnull), and a returned borrow is a pointer
// that is never null (returns_nonnull). `const` on the pointee is a DELIBERATE divergence —
// see annot_gate.sh's closing note — so it is not asserted here.
restrict
__attribute__((nonnull))
__attribute__((returns_nonnull))
